{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystalGradedDim","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystalGradedDim","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystal.demazure_droptop_exceeds_det_cap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystal.demazure_droptop_exceeds_det_cap","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DemazureSubcrystalGradedDim.lean#L88-L96","doc":"**The tightening is real and q-independent: the drop-top lower bracket still\nescapes the determinant cap.** For `q ≥ 1`, `[3]²_q ≥ 9 > 6 = C(4,2)`.  So the\nDAMPED Demazure A=4 object `[3]²_q` (lower bracket ≈ 11.17 at `q₀`) stays strictly\nabove the `SaturationRhoCap` ceiling `6` that the `−ln det` cumulant provably\ncannot clear — #4012's window `{6, [3][4]}` tightens to `{[3]², [3][4]}` with both\nends above the cap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystal.demazure_A4_droptop_le_full","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystal.demazure_A4_droptop_le_full","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DemazureSubcrystalGradedDim.lean#L78-L86","doc":"**A=4 bracket ordering: drop-top `[3]²_q ≤ [3]_q·[4]_q` = full.**\nThe two endpoints of the A=4 Demazure bracket (keep 3 vs 4 reps of the A3→A4\ncoset, holding A2→A3 full) are ordered for `q ≥ 1`.  The strong target `13.03`\nsits between them at the substrate `q₀` (`[3]²_{q₀} ≈ 11.17 < 13.03 < 15.74 ≈\n[3][4]_{q₀}`, the q₀-numeric bracket in the probe). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystal.q3_le_q4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystal.q3_le_q4","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DemazureSubcrystalGradedDim.lean#L71-L76","doc":"Full A=4 top-coset factor dominates the drop-top truncation: `[3]_q ≤ [4]_q`\nfor `q ≥ 1` (indeed `q ≥ 0`), since `[4]_q − [3]_q = q³ ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystal.demazure_A3_family_le_full","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystal.demazure_A3_family_le_full","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DemazureSubcrystalGradedDim.lean#L59-L69","doc":"**A=3 Demazure family is monotone in the truncation level: `1 ≤ [2]_q ≤ [3]_q`.**\nThe three A=3 truncations `{[1]_q, [2]_q, [3]_q} = {1, 1+q, 1+q+q²}` are ordered\nfor `q ≥ 1`, so the family MAXIMUM is the full ratio `[3]_q = ρ_grad(3)`.  A\nBruhat sub-sum cannot exceed the full sum — this is the A=3 obstruction: damping\nonly DECREASES `ρ(3)`, while the A=3 target sits ABOVE the full ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystal.q3_ge_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystal.q3_ge_three","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DemazureSubcrystalGradedDim.lean#L52-L57","doc":"Full `A=3` coset factor is `≥ 3` for `q ≥ 1` (equality at the classical\n`q = 1`, `3!/2! = 3`); the A=3 strong target `3.81` needs `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystal.q4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystal.q4","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DemazureSubcrystalGradedDim.lean#L49-L50","doc":"`[4]_q = 1 + q + q² + q³` — full `A=4` top-coset factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystal.q3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystal.q3","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DemazureSubcrystalGradedDim.lean#L46-L47","doc":"`[3]_q = 1 + q + q²` — full `A=3` coset factor / `ρ_grad(3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystal.q2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DemazureSubcrystal.q2","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DemazureSubcrystalGradedDim.lean#L43-L44","doc":"`[2]_q = 1 + q` — the `S_2/S_1` coset length-gen function (deuteron reference). ","signatureChunk":0}]}